    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Shakertowne lies in central Perry County, Missouri, and was settled in the late 1790s by families from Pennsylvania and Kentucky.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shakertowne_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits entirely on land, covering 1.32 square miles (3.42 km²) with no incorporated water bodies.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shakertowne_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Shakertowne experiences a humid continental climate, with hot, muggy summers and very cold, snowy winters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shakertowne_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area’s flood risk is moderate, with 19 properties projected to be affected over the next 30 years due to riverine overflow and heavy precipitation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/shakertowne_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Shakertowne’s elevation is about 600 feet (180 meters) above sea level, placing it on gently rolling uplands typical of the Ozark Border region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
